# Platform AI (Think)

Before changing anything AI-related, **read `docs/architecture/ai-think.md`.**
It records decisions made on 2026-09-28 that the schema alone does not show.

## Non-negotiables

1. The OpenAI key lives only in the Edge Function secret `OPENAI_API_KEY`.
   Never read it from `platform_config`, never ship it in a Flutter app, never commit it.
2. Apps never call OpenAI directly. Go through `ai_think`, `ai_memo_assist`, or another
   Edge Function that uses `_shared/ai/provider.ts`.
3. AI tools are read tools or propose tools, and go through RLS/RPC checks with the caller's JWT.
   A propose tool only inserts one `ai_actions` row via `ai_action_propose`; execution happens in
   `ai_action_apply` when the operator approves the card. Do not add a tool that executes a change,
   runs SQL, or touches the schema. New kinds of work = new `ai_actions.kind` + preview + apply branch.
   See `docs/architecture/ai-think-actions.md`.
4. Only a human action writes `ai_memories`. AI output is a draft until the operator
   presses approve. Never auto-promote a draft to `active`.
5. Model names, reasoning effort, token limits, and prices come from `_shared/ai/config.ts`
   (env overrides). Do not hardcode a model name at a call site.
6. Every AI call records one `ai_runs` row via `recordAiRun` (it never throws).
   Keep `feature` names stable; the usage screen groups by them.
7. Keep the context order in `ai_think/context.ts` stable (instructions, history,
   work-state note, relevant-memory note, current message). Reordering breaks prompt caching.
8. Update memories with the optimistic `version` check. An empty update result means
   someone else saved first; reload instead of overwriting.
9. Tests use `FakeAiProvider` (`AI_PROVIDER=fake`) and never assert exact AI wording.
10. Bump the `*_PROMPT_VERSION` constant in `ai_think/prompts.ts` or
    `ai_memo_assist/tasks.ts` when a prompt changes.
11. The conversation tree (`ai_tree_nodes`) is not answer context. The only AI read is the
    `list_tree_folders` tool: folder ids/titles/parents and conversation placement, plus conversation
    titles via `list_conversations`. Never expose excerpt titles, summaries, or message text.
    Messages with `context_excluded = true` must stay out of every AI read path
    (`store.listMessages` is the single place that reads messages for AI).
12. Keep code diffs out of AI context. Store queries select individual `result` fields
    (`ai_think/store.ts` `ROUND_COLUMNS`); only the code review sees a clipped diff head.

## Code investigation (Think ↔ Cursor)

Design and current phase: `docs/architecture/ai-code-bridge.md`.

- Investigate and plan runs (`mode = 'investigate' | 'plan'`) get read tools only (`read`, `grep`, `glob`, `ls`, SDK mode `plan`).
  Change runs (`mode = 'change'`) add `edit` and `delete` only, run in an isolated git worktree of a
  working-tree snapshot, and set `CODE_BRIDGE_WRITE_ROOT` so the hook blocks every path outside it.
  Never add shell, MCP, PR, commit, or push tools. The real working folder changes only through an
  approved apply job (`git apply --check` first, backup ref before, revert with `-R`).
- `CURSOR_API_KEY` and `CODE_BRIDGE_WORKER_TOKEN` live only in the operator PC's environment.
  The server keeps only `CODE_BRIDGE_WORKER_TOKEN_SHA256`. Never put either in an app, the DB, or git.
- Request state changes go through the `ai_code_request_*` (app) and `ai_code_bridge_*` (worker,
  service role) RPCs. The app writes only draft `title` and `request`.
- `.cursor/hooks/deny-secrets.mjs` must stay fail-closed. Korean Windows can hand it input with
  quotes eaten after Korean text; it then checks path fields only. Keep its tests in
  `tools/code_bridge/test/deny_secrets.test.mjs` passing. The `preToolUse` matcher must include
  `Write|Delete` (that is how the SDK reports edits and deletes).
- Code review (`ai_code_bridge/code_review.ts`) posts at most one assistant message per request and
  asks follow-up rounds only while round < max_rounds (investigate: 2, plan: 3). It never applies anything.
- Code changes go through coordination: Think calls `start_code_plan`, which starts a read-only plan
  request without approval (the one exception to propose-then-approve; it still counts against the daily
  limit and is recorded as an `applied` `code_plan` action). After the last round, the review proposes a
  `code_change` action (`payload.plan_request_id`) — the 조율본 — that the operator must approve, and the
  resulting diff still needs a second approval to apply. Do not let plan mode edit files or skip either approval.
- Unresolved points in a 조율본 are `spec.decisions` (multiple choice, recommended option first). The operator
  answers them in the card; `ai_code_plan_revise` records the answers as `owner_answers` plus
  "운영자 결정 — " constraints and re-runs one plan round. Keep those constraints when writing a new 조율본,
  and never treat a recommended option as the operator's answer.

## Out of scope unless the user asks

Autonomous DB writes, auto-running migrations, arbitrary SQL, Codex integration,
vector databases, complex model routers, unapproved code edits, commits or PRs by the Cursor agent.
Multi-agent work is limited to the code bridge above.
